# Learn2Drive Mobile — Cursor Rules

You are building Learn2Drive, a Nigeria-focused React Native app connecting learners with FRSC-approved driving schools.

## Documentation First

Before implementing features, read:
- `project_plan.md` — master plan
- `docs/architecture.md` — system design
- `docs/decisions.md` — ADRs (do not contradict without updating ADRs)

Expo SDK 56 docs: https://docs.expo.dev/versions/v56.0.0/

## Mandatory Stack

- React Native 0.79+ / Expo SDK 56
- TypeScript (strict)
- NativeWind (styling — prefer `className` over large StyleSheet)
- Expo Router (file-based routing; Stack/Tabs in `_layout.tsx`)
- TanStack Query v5 (server state)
- Zustand (client state only)
- React Hook Form + Zod (all forms)
- react-native-maps
- socket.io-client
- expo-notifications
- expo-secure-store (JWT)
- expo-location (GPS)

Do NOT introduce Redux, MobX, Apollo, or alternative form libraries.

## State Management (Strict)

### TanStack Query ONLY for:
- Auth API requests
- Driving schools, instructors, vehicles
- Bookings, sessions, reviews
- User profile (server-fetched)

Never store server/API cache in Zustand.

### Zustand ONLY for:
- Auth state (tokens, isAuthenticated)
- User session snapshot (id, role)
- selectedSchool, selectedPackage
- activeSession, currentCoordinates
- UI state, theme, app settings

Never use Zustand for API caching.

## Folder Structure

Expo Router owns navigation. Place code only in:

```
src/app/                    # Routes only (Expo Router file-based routing)
src/components/{common,forms,cards,maps}/
src/hooks/
src/api/
src/services/
src/store/
src/types/
src/utils/
src/constants/
src/lib/
```

### Expo Router conventions (`src/app/`)

| Pattern | Example | URL |
|---------|---------|-----|
| Route group | `(auth)/login.tsx` | `/login` |
| Index route | `(auth)/index.tsx` | `/` |
| Layout | `(auth)/_layout.tsx` | defines stack/tabs for group |
| Dynamic | `schools/[id].tsx` | `/schools/123` |
| Not found | `+not-found.tsx` | catch-all |

- **Do not** create `src/screens/`, `src/features/`, or `src/navigation/`.
- Route files are thin when possible; screen-specific UI can live directly in `src/app/` routes.
- `src/components/` — **reusable** UI only (buttons, cards, form fields). No screen-specific layouts.
- `src/api/` — HTTP client, endpoints, query keys, query hooks.
- `src/services/` — socket, notifications, location, secure storage.

## Navigation & RBAC

Roles: `learner` | `guardian` | `instructor` | `school_admin` | `platform_admin`

After auth, redirect to exactly ONE role route group via root `_layout.tsx` (role resolver).
Never expose routes from other roles to unauthenticated or wrong-role users.
Auth routes in `src/app/(auth)/`: splash (`index`), login, register, forgot-password.
Role routes in `src/app/(learner)/`, `(guardian)/`, `(instructor)/`, `(school)/`, `(admin)/`.

## Authentication

- JWT access + refresh tokens in expo-secure-store
- Bearer token on API requests via axios/fetch interceptor
- Role-based route protection at navigator level

## Components & Code Style

- Functional components only
- Absolute imports: `@/...` (never deep relative `../../../`)
- Small, reusable components in `src/components/`
- Custom hooks for reusable logic (`useXxx`)
- No prop drilling — use hooks, context sparingly, or Zustand for UI
- SOLID / Clean Architecture where practical
- ESLint + Prettier compliant

## Forms

Always: React Hook Form + Zod schemas.
Never: useState for form field values (except trivial toggles).

## Styling

- NativeWind `className` tokens
- Design tokens from `src/constants/theme.ts`: primary, secondary, success, warning, error
- Pill buttons: set `borderRadius: borderRadius.button` + `overflow: 'hidden'` in `style` (Android needs this; `rounded-button` alone may not apply on Pressable)
- Mobile-first, accessible labels and touch targets (min 44pt)

## Maps & Realtime

- react-native-maps for schools, routes, live tracking
- socket.io-client in `src/services/socket.ts` for session events and location broadcast

## Error Handling

- Error boundaries for render failures
- Query error/loading/empty states on all data screens
- Zod validation messages on forms
- NetInfo offline indicator where appropriate

## Testing

Structure tests under `__tests__/` mirroring `src/`.
Use Jest + React Native Testing Library when adding tests.

## Environment

- Secrets in `.env` (never commit)
- Use `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` for client-safe config
- Reference `.env.example` for required variables

## What NOT To Do

- Do not add server state to Zustand
- Do not create forms with raw useState
- Do not bypass RBAC with direct navigation to role screens
- Do not store tokens in AsyncStorage
- Do not add dependencies outside the approved stack without an ADR in `docs/decisions.md`
- Do not create markdown files unless explicitly requested
